        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Several precise mechanics, a required toy and a nine-orb jumping challenge; a small coordinated group helps.\n\n1. Before entering, ensure someone has the Mrgrglhjorn toy from No Shellfish Endeavor. Choose Normal Tomb of Sargeras for the straightforward mechanics. Remove passive damage effects and unnecessary weapons for the achievements that require preserving low-health bosses / adds. Enter at the Broken Shore's north end, around 64,21.5.\n\n2. Goroth - Fel Turkey!: stop damaging the boss after pulling. Keep him away from Infernal Spikes, using a passive tanking pet if available. Bait spikes in a line, move Crashing Comet away from them, then stand behind them when Shattering Star targets you. Count at least 30 spikes destroyed specifically by Shattering Star; spikes removed by Burning, walking or Comet do not count. Survive the enrage with healing, then kill Goroth.\n\n3. Demonic Inquisition - Grin and Bear It: lower the bosses without killing them, then stop and gain 100 Torment, attacking during their special damage-reflection abilities if needed. Every living participant needs maximum Torment at the kill. Do not use Confess to clear it at the end. With maximum Torment direct attacks often miss; a pet, damage-over-time or suitable area attack can finish the bosses.\n\n4. Harjatan - Grand Fin-ale: engage Harjatan gently FIRST, then use Mrgrglhjorn and let Elder Murk-Eye appear. Kill Elder Murk-Eye before Harjatan. Using the toy before combat wastes its long cooldown; killing Harjatan with passive damage before the add spawns also fails the sequence.\n\n5. Mistress Sassz'ine - Five Course Seafood Buffet: preserve a Razorjaw Waverunner murloc from phase one by releasing it with a jellyfish stun / dispel. Reduce it below 10% without killing it. Push the boss into the Sarukel phase, keeping her above 40%. Feed Sarukel the weakened murloc and an Abyss Stalker in the outer maw circle; let him consume them rather than killing them yourself. Take Hydra Shot in the outer circle, bring Befouling Ink into the maw, and briefly enter the inner circle for Player Seasoning, escaping with movement / a defensive or letting a volunteer die. Finish only after all five foods count; keep a second player alive if sacrificing someone.\n\n6. Sisters of the Moon - Wax On, Wax Off: bring the isolated Twilight Soul from the left side of the preceding trash hall into the boss room alive. Lower the Sisters to about 20% without cleaving the soul. Once the soul changes from purple to BLUE, kill the soul first and then the Sisters. Its name does not change; moving it through moon colors for several minutes is unnecessary.\n\n7. The Desolate Host - Great Soul, Great Purpose: engage and catch the first yellow falling soul directly underneath the Engine of Souls. At modern damage, quickly finish the Engine and then the Desolate Host before the soul drops; allow the Host to actually spawn before the killing burst. For a longer fight, use four catchers, two per realm, alternating corporeal 1, spirit 1, corporeal 2, spirit 2 into each yellow landing circle. Never let the soul hit the floor.\n\n8. Maiden of Vigilance - Sky Walker: collect ALL NINE Titanic Anomalies before killing her: first the central orb inside the well, then four lower orbs, then four above the platform. Obtain Unstable Soul by touching the opposite light / fel mechanic. Time the explosion to launch you back from the well or upward into high orbs. A mobile character such as a Demon Hunter can aim with mid-air movement; a second player keeps the boss engaged during attempts. Avoid passive damage while practicing. If Normal's automatic slow fall interferes, Heroic removes it but requires more careful timing. Remove the shield and interrupt her during the encounter as necessary.\n\n9. Fallen Avatar - Bingo!: damage the Avatar, allow the scripted floor break, then burst him on the lower platform while preserving an entire row and column of tiles. Tank him in a corner if another Rupture Realities is imminent so it removes as little floor as possible. The row and column criteria can be earned on separate kills if needed.\n\n10. Kil'jaeden - Dark Souls: let the initial flying intermission finish and wait for him to land. Burst through the later 40% Deceiver's Veil transition before any Shadowsoul completes Destabilized Shadowsoul. If the adds do spawn, find Illidan for sight and kill / stun them before their casts complete. Rushing from the opening into overlapping invulnerable flight phases can prevent the clean burst.\n\n11. Complete the nine achievement criteria across your runs, then collect the Glory reward and learn Micronax. The meta still awards the pet even if a UI preview displays only the Tomb Raider title; it is not a random raid-boss pet drop.",
        tips = "",
